-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(e)(6): the excess shelter expense deduction, the standard utility allowance, the homeless shelter deduction, internet fees;
-- and the order in which the deductions of subsection (e) produce the household's net income.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 2012(j) (elderly or disabled member), s 2012(l) (every member a homeless individual).

§ `s 2014(e)(6) Excess shelter expense deduction`

-- Maximum excess shelter deductions, FY 2027 (USDA Table 3, line 85): a monthly dollar cap per place, for a household with no elderly or disabled member.
`s 2014(e)(6)(B) maximum excess shelter deduction, FY 2027` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 769, 1229, 1229, 1229, 903, 1306, 606

-- Homeless shelter deduction, FY 2027 (USDA Table 4, line 89): the same figure in every place.
`s 2014(e)(6)(D) homeless shelter deduction, FY 2027` MEANS 205.66

-- Maximum asset limits, FY 2027 (USDA Table 5, line 93).
`s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, FY 2027` MEANS 4750
`s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for all other households, FY 2027` MEANS 3000

-- src:310 | A household shall be entitled, with respect to expenses other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, to an excess shelter expense deduction to the extent that the monthly amount expended by a household for shelter exceeds an amount equal to 50 percent of monthly household income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(A) (src:310)
GIVEN `the monthly amount expended by the household for shelter, other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly household income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6)(A) the excess shelter expense deduction before the maximum` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, `the monthly amount expended by the household for shelter, other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, in dollars` MINUS (50% TIMES `the monthly household income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed, in dollars`))

-- The maximum of subparagraph (B), for a household that does not contain an elderly or disabled individual. The result names the three cases the text
-- distinguishes: a dollar cap; no cap stated (the household contains an elderly or disabled individual); and a cap this text does not give.
DECLARE `s 2014(e)(6)(B) the cap` IS ONE OF
    `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` HAS `s 2014(e)(6)(B) dollars a month` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2014(e)(6)(B) no cap stated for the household`
    `s 2014(e)(6)(B) cap not covered by this text`

-- The figures of clauses (i) to (v), "respectively" for the 48 States and DC, Alaska, Hawaii, Guam and the Virgin Islands.
-- Ruler (the core's order): the 48 States and DC, Alaska urban, rural 1, rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands.
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(i) maximum, 22 August 1996 to 31 December 1996` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 247, 429, 429, 429, 300, 353, 182
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(ii) maximum, 1 January 1997 to 30 September 1998` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 250, 434, 434, 434, 304, 357, 184
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(iii) maximum, fiscal year 1999` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 275, 478, 478, 478, 334, 393, 203
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(iv) maximum, fiscal year 2000` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 280, 483, 483, 483, 339, 398, 208
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(v) maximum, fiscal year 2001` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 340, 543, 543, 543, 399, 458, 268

-- src:311 | (B) Maximum amount of deduction
-- src:312 | In the case of a household that does not contain an elderly or disabled individual, in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, and the Virgin Islands of the United States, the excess shelter expense deduction shall not exceed—
-- src:313 | (i) for the period beginning on August 22, 1996, and ending on December 31, 1996, $247, $429, $353, $300, and $182 per month, respectively;
-- src:314 | (ii) for the period beginning on January 1, 1997, and ending on September 30, 1998, $250, $434, $357, $304, and $184 per month, respectively;
-- src:315 | (iii) for fiscal year 1999, $275, $478, $393, $334, and $203 per month, respectively;
-- src:316 | (iv) for fiscal year 2000, $280, $483, $398, $339, and $208 per month, respectively;
-- src:317 | (v) for fiscal year 2001, $340, $543, $458, $399, and $268 per month, respectively; and
-- src:318 | (vi) for fiscal year 2002 and each subsequent fiscal year, the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as adjusted to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(B), the maximum amount (src:311-318)
GIVEN `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      area IS AN Area
GIVETH A `s 2014(e)(6)(B) the cap`
`s 2014(e)(6)(B) the maximum excess shelter expense deduction on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) no cap stated for the household`  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the maximum is "In the case of a household that does not contain an elderly or disabled individual"
        IF NOT (`snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`)
            THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) cap not covered by this text`  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household contains an elderly or disabled individual was not supplied
        IF day LESS THAN Date 22 8 1996 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) cap not covered by this text`  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): clause (i) begins on August 22, 1996
        IF day AT MOST Date 31 12 1996 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B)(i) maximum, 22 August 1996 to 31 December 1996` area)
        IF day AT MOST Date 30 9 1998 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B)(ii) maximum, 1 January 1997 to 30 September 1998` area)
        IF day AT MOST Date 30 9 1999 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B)(iii) maximum, fiscal year 1999` area)
        IF day AT MOST Date 30 9 2000 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B)(iv) maximum, fiscal year 2000` area)
        IF day AT MOST Date 30 9 2001 THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B)(v) maximum, fiscal year 2001` area)
        IF day AT LEAST Date 1 10 2026 AND day AT MOST Date 30 9 2027
            THEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` `s 2014(e)(6)(B) maximum excess shelter deduction, FY 2027` area)
        OTHERWISE `s 2014(e)(6)(B) cap not covered by this text`  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): clause (vi) indexes the amount every year by the Consumer Price Index; only the fiscal year 2027 figure was supplied

-- src:318 | (vi) for fiscal year 2002 and each subsequent fiscal year, the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as adjusted to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(B)(vi) (src:318)
GIVEN `the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6)(B)(vi) the maximum after indexing` MEANS
    `the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction`)

-- src:309 | (A) In general
-- src:310 | A household shall be entitled, with respect to expenses other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, to an excess shelter expense deduction to the extent that the monthly amount expended by a household for shelter exceeds an amount equal to 50 percent of monthly household income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed.
-- src:311 | (B) Maximum amount of deduction
-- src:312 | In the case of a household that does not contain an elderly or disabled individual, in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, and the Virgin Islands of the United States, the excess shelter expense deduction shall not exceed—
-- src:313 | (i) for the period beginning on August 22, 1996, and ending on December 31, 1996, $247, $429, $353, $300, and $182 per month, respectively;
-- src:314 | (ii) for the period beginning on January 1, 1997, and ending on September 30, 1998, $250, $434, $357, $304, and $184 per month, respectively;
-- src:315 | (iii) for fiscal year 1999, $275, $478, $393, $334, and $203 per month, respectively;
-- src:316 | (iv) for fiscal year 2000, $280, $483, $398, $339, and $208 per month, respectively;
-- src:317 | (v) for fiscal year 2001, $340, $543, $458, $399, and $268 per month, respectively; and
-- src:318 | (vi) for fiscal year 2002 and each subsequent fiscal year, the applicable amount during the preceding fiscal year, as adjusted to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(A) and (B), the deduction after the maximum (src:309-318)
GIVEN `the deduction before the maximum, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      cap IS A `s 2014(e)(6)(B) the cap`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6) the excess shelter expense deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER cap
        WHEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` c THEN JUST (minimum (LIST `the deduction before the maximum, in dollars`, c))
        WHEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) no cap stated for the household` THEN JUST `the deduction before the maximum, in dollars`
        WHEN `s 2014(e)(6)(B) cap not covered by this text` THEN NOTHING

-- (C) The standard utility allowance.
-- src:321 | a State agency may use a standard utility allowance in accordance with regulations promulgated by the Secretary, subject to clause (iv), except that a State agency may use an allowance that does not fluctuate within a year to reflect seasonal variations.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(i) (src:321)
GIVEN `the allowance is in accordance with regulations promulgated by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowance does not fluctuate within a year to reflect seasonal variations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(i) the State agency may use the standard utility allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the allowance is in accordance with regulations promulgated by the Secretary` OR `the allowance does not fluctuate within a year to reflect seasonal variations`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a State agency may use a standard utility allowance in accordance with regulations ... except that a State agency may use an allowance that does not fluctuate within a year"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "in accordance with regulations promulgated by the Secretary", subject to clause (iv)

-- src:322 | (ii) Restrictions on heating and cooling expenses
-- src:323 | An allowance for a heating or cooling expense may not be used in the case of a household that—
-- src:324 | (I) does not incur a heating or cooling expense, as the case may be;
-- src:325 | (II) does incur a heating or cooling expense but is located in a public housing unit that has central utility meters and charges households, with regard to the expense, only for excess utility costs; or
-- src:326 | (III) shares the expense with, and lives with, another individual not participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, another household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, or both, unless the allowance is prorated between the household and the other individual, household, or both.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(ii), restrictions on heating and cooling expenses (src:322-326)
-- src:334 | (III) Inapplicability of certain restrictions
-- src:335 | Clauses (ii)(II) and (ii)(III) shall not apply in the case of a State agency that has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under subclause (I).
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iii)(III), inapplicability of certain restrictions (src:334-335)
GIVEN `the household incurs a heating or cooling expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is located in a public housing unit that has central utility meters and charges households, with regard to the expense, only for excess utility costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household shares the expense with, and lives with, another individual not participating in the program, another household participating in the program, or both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowance is prorated between the household and the other individual, household, or both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under clause (iii)(I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(ii) an allowance for a heating or cooling expense may be used` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household incurs a heating or cooling expense`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An allowance for a heating or cooling expense may not be used in the case of a household that— (I) does not incur a heating or cooling expense"
        IF `the household is located in a public housing unit that has central utility meters and charges households, with regard to the expense, only for excess utility costs` AND (NOT `the State agency has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under clause (iii)(I)`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An allowance for a heating or cooling expense may not be used in the case of a household that— ... (II) does incur a heating or cooling expense but is located in a public housing unit that has central utility meters"
        IF `the household shares the expense with, and lives with, another individual not participating in the program, another household participating in the program, or both` AND (NOT `the allowance is prorated between the household and the other individual, household, or both`) AND (NOT `the State agency has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under clause (iii)(I)`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(III) shares the expense with, and lives with, another individual ... unless the allowance is prorated"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii) says when an allowance may not be used; it does not say that it may be used in any other case

-- src:327 | (iii) Mandatory allowance
-- src:328 | (I) In general
-- src:329 | A State agency may make the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory for all households with qualifying utility costs if—
-- src:330 | (aa) the State agency has developed 1 or more standards that include the cost of heating and cooling and 1 or more standards that do not include the cost of heating and cooling; and
-- src:331 | (bb) the Secretary finds (without regard to subclause (III)) that the standards will not result in an increased cost to the Secretary.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iii)(I) (src:327-331)
GIVEN `the State agency has developed 1 or more standards that include the cost of heating and cooling and 1 or more standards that do not include the cost of heating and cooling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary finds that the standards will not result in an increased cost to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iii)(I) the State agency may make the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has developed 1 or more standards that include the cost of heating and cooling and 1 or more standards that do not include the cost of heating and cooling` AND `the Secretary finds that the standards will not result in an increased cost to the Secretary`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "may make the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory for all households with qualifying utility costs if— (aa) ...; and (bb) ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the power is given "if" both (aa) and (bb) hold (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:332 | (II) Household election
-- src:333 | A State agency that has not made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under subclause (I) shall allow a household to switch, at the end of a certification period, between the standard utility allowance and a deduction based on the actual utility costs of the household.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iii)(II) (src:332-333)
GIVEN `the State agency has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the end of a certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iii)(II) the household may switch between the standard utility allowance and actual utility costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the State agency has made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory under subclause (I)`) AND `it is the end of a certification period`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall allow a household to switch, at the end of a certification period, between the standard utility allowance and a deduction based on the actual utility costs"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A State agency that has not made the use of a standard utility allowance mandatory" and runs "at the end of a certification period"

-- src:338 | if a State agency elects to use a standard utility allowance that reflects heating and cooling costs, the standard utility allowance shall be made available to households with an elderly or disabled member that received a payment, or on behalf of which a payment was made, under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981 (42 U.S.C. 8621 et seq.) or other similar energy assistance program, if in the current month or in the immediately preceding 12 months, the household either received such a payment, or such a payment was made on behalf of the household, that was greater than $20 annually, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(I) (src:338)
GIVEN `the State agency elects to use a standard utility allowance that reflects heating and cooling costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household received a payment, or a payment was made on its behalf, under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981 or another similar energy assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the current month or in the immediately preceding 12 months the payments were greater than $20 annually, as determined by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(I) the standard utility allowance must be made available to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency elects to use a standard utility allowance that reflects heating and cooling costs`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "if a State agency elects to use a standard utility allowance that reflects heating and cooling costs" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed "to households with an elderly or disabled member"
        IF NOT (`the household received a payment, or a payment was made on its behalf, under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981 or another similar energy assistance program` AND `in the current month or in the immediately preceding 12 months the payments were greater than $20 annually, as determined by the Secretary`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is "if in the current month or in the immediately preceding 12 months the household either received such a payment ... that was greater than $20 annually" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the standard utility allowance shall be made available to households with an elderly or disabled member that received a payment"

-- src:339 | (II) Separate allowance
-- src:340 | A State agency may use a separate standard utility allowance for households on behalf of which a payment described in subclause (I) is made, but may not be required to do so.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(II) (src:339-340)
GIVEN `the State agency is required to use a separate standard utility allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(II) the State agency may be required to use a separate standard utility allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency is required to use a separate standard utility allowance` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but may not be required to do so"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on being "required" to use a separate allowance; the State agency "may use" one

-- src:342 | A State agency that does not elect to use a separate allowance but makes a single standard utility allowance available to households incurring heating or cooling expenses (other than a household described in subclause (I) or (II) of clause (ii)) may not be required to reduce the allowance due to the provision (directly or indirectly) of assistance under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(III) (src:342)
GIVEN `the State agency does not elect to use a separate allowance but makes a single standard utility allowance available to households incurring heating or cooling expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(III) the State agency may be required to reduce the allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency does not elect to use a separate allowance but makes a single standard utility allowance available to households incurring heating or cooling expenses`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): such a State agency "may not be required to reduce the allowance due to the provision (directly or indirectly) of assistance under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a State agency that "does not elect to use a separate allowance but makes a single standard utility allowance available"

-- src:344 | assistance provided under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981 (42 U.S.C. 8621 et seq.) shall be considered to be prorated over the entire heating or cooling season for which the assistance was provided.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(IV) (src:344)
GIVEN `the assistance provided under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the entire heating or cooling season for which the assistance was provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6)(C)(iv)(IV) the monthly amount of the energy assistance prorated over the season` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of months in the entire heating or cooling season for which the assistance was provided` AT MOST 0
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a season of no months cannot be prorated over
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the assistance provided under the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Act of 1981, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the number of months in the entire heating or cooling season for which the assistance was provided`)

-- (D) Homeless households.
-- src:346 | (i) Alternative deduction
-- src:347 | The State agency shall allow a deduction of $143 a month for households—
-- src:348 | (I) in which all members are homeless individuals;
-- src:349 | (II) that are not receiving free shelter throughout the month; and
-- src:350 | (III) that do not opt to claim an excess shelter expense deduction under subparagraph (A).
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(D)(i), the alternative deduction (src:346-350)
-- src:353 | (iii) Ineligibility
-- src:354 | The State agency may make a household with extremely low shelter costs ineligible for the alternative deduction under clause (i).
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(D)(iii), ineligibility (src:353-354)
GIVEN `s 2012(l) every member of the household is a homeless individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household is receiving free shelter throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household opts to claim an excess shelter expense deduction under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has made the household ineligible for the alternative deduction because of extremely low shelter costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(D) the household is entitled to the homeless shelter deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has made the household ineligible for the alternative deduction because of extremely low shelter costs`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The State agency may make a household with extremely low shelter costs ineligible for the alternative deduction under clause (i)"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(l) every member of the household is a homeless individual` AND (NOT `the household is receiving free shelter throughout the month`) AND (NOT `the household opts to claim an excess shelter expense deduction under subparagraph (A)`)
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The State agency shall allow a deduction of $143 a month for households— (I) in which all members are homeless individuals; (II) that are not receiving free shelter throughout the month; and (III) that do not opt to claim an excess shelter expense deduction"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deduction is for households that meet (I), (II) and (III); the text is silent on the others (section 2012(l) is a seam input)

-- src:347 | The State agency shall allow a deduction of $143 a month for households—
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(D)(i), the amount (src:347)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6)(D) the homeless shelter deduction for the fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year` LESS THAN 2019 THEN JUST 143
        IF `the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027 THEN JUST `s 2014(e)(6)(D) homeless shelter deduction, FY 2027`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): clause (ii) adjusts the $143 every year from fiscal year 2019 by the Consumer Price Index; only the fiscal year 2027 figure was supplied

-- src:351 | (ii) Adjustment
-- src:352 | For fiscal year 2019 and each subsequent fiscal year the amount of the homeless shelter deduction specified in clause (i) shall be adjusted to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(D)(ii) (src:351-352)
GIVEN `the homeless shelter deduction of the preceding fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(6)(D)(ii) the adjusted homeless shelter deduction` MEANS
    `the homeless shelter deduction of the preceding fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding November 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction`)

-- (E) Internet expenses.
