@ref s 2014(e)(6)(E) (src:355-356)
GIVEN `the expense is a service fee associated with internet connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(6)(E) the expense is used in computing the excess shelter expense deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the expense is a service fee associated with internet connection`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any service fee associated with internet connection shall not be used in computing the excess shelter expense deduction"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subparagraph (E) bars internet service fees only; whether another expense is a shelter expense is not answered here

§ `s 2014(e) Net income`

-- The order of the computation: every deduction other than the shelter deduction first, because paragraph (6)(A) measures shelter against "monthly household
-- income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed", and the child support deduction is determined before the shelter deduction (paragraph (4)(B)).
-- The text does not say that income after deductions cannot fall below zero (finding F-E2): this function does not floor it.
-- src:252 | (1) Standard deduction
-- src:253 | (A) In general
-- src:254 | (i) Deduction
@ref s 2014(e), deductions from income (src:252-254)
GIVEN `the household's income after the exclusions of subsection (d), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the standard deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the earned income deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the dependent care deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the child support deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the excess medical expense deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e) the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction` MEANS
    `the household's income after the exclusions of subsection (d), in dollars` MINUS (`the standard deduction, in dollars` PLUS `the earned income deduction, in dollars` PLUS `the dependent care deduction, in dollars` PLUS `the child support deduction, in dollars` PLUS `the excess medical expense deduction, in dollars`)

-- src:309 | (A) In general
-- src:310 | A household shall be entitled, with respect to expenses other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, to an excess shelter expense deduction to the extent that the monthly amount expended by a household for shelter exceeds an amount equal to 50 percent of monthly household income after all other applicable deductions have been allowed.
@ref s 2014(e)(6)(A), the shelter deduction comes last (src:309-310)
GIVEN `the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the excess shelter expense deduction` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e) the household's net income` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the excess shelter expense deduction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the shelter deduction was not determined (no maximum for the date, or the elderly or disabled question not supplied)
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction, in dollars` MINUS d)
